rand_P...</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>1</th>\n      <td>2</td>\n      <td>sepang</td>\n      <td>Sepang International Circuit</td>\n      <td>Kuala Lumpur</td>\n      <td>Malaysia</td>\n      <td>2.76083</td>\n      <td>101.73800</td>\n      <td>18</td>\n      <td>http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sepang_Internatio...</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>2</th>\n      <td>3</td>\n      <td>bahrain</td>\n      <td>Bahrain International Circuit</td>\n      <td>Sakhir</td>\n      <td>Bahrain</td>\n      <td>26.03250</td>\n      <td>50.51060</td>\n      <td>7</td>\n      <td>http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bahrain_Internati...</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>3</th>\n      <td>4</td>\n      <td>catalunya</td>\n      <td>Circuit de Barcelona-Catalunya</td>\n      <td>Montmeló</td>\n      <td>Spain</td>\n      <td>41.57000</td>\n      <td>2.26111</td>\n      <td>109</td>\n      <td>http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circuit_de_Barcel...</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>4</th>\n      <td>5</td>\n      <td>istanbul</td>\n      <td>Istanbul Park</td>\n      <td>Istanbul</td>\n      <td>Turkey</td>\n      <td>40.95170</td>\n      <td>29.40500</td>\n      <td>130</td>\n      <td>http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Istanbul_Park</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":"<class 'pandas.core.frame.DataFrame'>\nRangeIndex: 77 entries, 0 to 76\nData columns (total 9 columns):\n #   Column      Non-Null Count  Dtype  \n---  ------      --------------  -----  \n 0   circuitId   77 non-null     int64  \n 1   circuitRef  77 non-null     object \n 2   name        77 non-null     object \n 3   location    77 non-null     object \n 4   country     77 non-null     object \n 5   lat         77 non-null     float64\n 6   lng         77 non-null     float64\n 7   alt         77 non-null     int64  \n 8   url         77 non-null     object \ndtypes: float64(2), int64(2), object(5)\nmemory usage: 5.5+ KB\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":2},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**circuits** has one row per circuit, 77 in total, describing where races are held:\n\n- **circuitId:** the number that identifies each circuit. Other tables (we expect `races`) use it to say where a race took place.\n- **circuitRef:** a short text name for the circuit (e.g. `albert_park`), another identifier.\n- **name:** the full official name of the circuit.\n- **location:** the city or area where the circuit is (e.g. Melbourne).\n- **country:** the country of the circuit, written as a country name (e.g. Australia, Spain).\n- **lat / lng:** the circuit's geographic coordinates.\n- **alt:** the circuit's altitude, in metres, above sea level.\n- **url:** the circuit's Wikipedia page.\n\n**What we notice**\n\n1) **Types:** `lat` and `lng` were read as decimal numbers (`float64`), and `alt` and `circuitId` as whole numbers (`int64`). pandas stores a whole column as text (`object`) if even one value in it is not a number, such as the `\\N` placeholder. Since these four columns came out as numbers, none of them contains a placeholder. The non-null counts in `.info()` are all 77, but at this stage that does not mean nothing is missing: we loaded the data without letting pandas mark anything as missing, so a `\\N` is counted as a normal value. The audit (1.3) counts the placeholders directly.\n\n2) **country** is the column that matters most here. Data-engineering Question 2 compares races in a driver's home country with races elsewhere. In the rows shown, countries are written as names (Australia, Spain, Turkey). The F1 introduction mentions that drivers' nationality is stored differently, as an adjective such as \"British\". We check this when we reach `drivers`; if the two are written differently, we will need a mapping between them for Question 2.\n\n3) **circuitId** is needed for Question 1, which asks at which circuits a front-row start (grid 1 or 2) most often turns into a podium. To answer it, we compute that rate separately for each circuit, so every result must be linked to the circuit where the race took place, through `circuitId`.\n\n4) **Available before the race?** Yes. A circuit is a fixed fact about the race known long in advance, so nothing in this table is leakage. `lat`, `lng`, `alt`, `url` and `circuitRef` are descriptive and not needed for any of our questions.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**How are countries written?** The first rows only show 5 of the 77 circuits. Since Question 2 depends on matching circuit countries to driver nationalities, each country has to be written in exactly one way: if the same country appeared under two different names, it would be counted as two separate countries. We list every distinct value to check.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"print(df[\"country\"].nunique(), \"different country values\")\nprint(sorted(df[\"country\"].unique()))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.238592Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.238862Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.246061Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.238839Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.244968Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"35 different country values\n['Argentina', 'Australia', 'Austria', 'Azerbaijan', 'Bahrain', 'Belgium', 'Brazil', 'Canada', 'China', 'France', 'Germany', 'Hungary', 'India', 'Italy', 'Japan', 'Korea', 'Malaysia', 'Mexico', 'Monaco', 'Morocco', 'Netherlands', 'Portugal', 'Qatar', 'Russia', 'Saudi Arabia', 'Singapore', 'South Africa', 'Spain', 'Sweden', 'Switzerland', 'Turkey', 'UAE', 'UK', 'USA', 'United States']\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":3},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"There are 35 distinct country values, and the United States appears under two labels: `USA` and `United States`. Grouping by country as it stands would split the US into two countries. Most countries are written as full names, but a few use short forms (`UK`, `UAE`). `UK` is also the form the F1 introduction uses as its example. We look at which circuits carry each of the two US labels.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"df[df[\"country\"].isin([\"USA\", \"United States\"])][[\"circuitId\", \"name\", \"location\", \"country\"]]","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.247237Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.247528Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.27737Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.247504Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.276533Z"}},"outputs":[{"execution_count":4,"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":"    circuitId                             name        location        country\n18         19      Indianapolis Motor Speedway    Indianapolis            USA\n22         80   Las Vegas Strip Street Circuit       Las Vegas  United States\n32         33           Phoenix street circuit         Phoenix            USA\n36         37           Detroit Street Circuit         Detroit            USA\n41         42                        Fair Park          Dallas            USA\n42         43                       Long Beach      California            USA\n43         44         Las Vegas Street Circuit          Nevada            USA\n45         46                     Watkins Glen  New York State            USA\n59         60  Riverside International Raceway      California            USA\n62         63    Sebring International Raceway         Florida            USA\n68         69          Circuit of the Americas          Austin            USA\n76         79    Miami International Autodrome           Miami            USA","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>circuitId</th>\n      <th>name</th>\n      <th>location</th>\n      <th>country</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>18</th>\n      <td>19</td>\n      <td>Indianapolis Motor Speedway</td>\n      <td>Indianapolis</td>\n      <td>USA</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>22</th>\n      <td>80</td>\n      <td>Las Vegas Strip Street Circuit</td>\n      <td>Las Vegas</td>\n      <td>United States</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>32</th>\n      <td>33</td>\n      <td>Phoenix street circuit</td>\n      <td>Phoenix</td>\n      <td>USA</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>36</th>\n      <td>37</td>\n      <td>Detroit Street Circuit</td>\n      <td>Detroit</td>\n      <td>USA</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>41</th>\n      <td>42</td>\n      <td>Fair Park</td>\n      <td>Dallas</td>\n      <td>USA</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>42</th>\n      <td>43</td>\n      <td>Long Beach</td>\n      <td>California</td>\n      <td>USA</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>43</th>\n      <td>44</td>\n      <td>Las Vegas Street Circuit</td>\n      <td>Nevada</td>\n      <td>USA</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>45</th>\n      <td>46</td>\n      <td>Watkins Glen</td>\n      <td>New York State</td>\n      <td>USA</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>59</th>\n      <td>60</td>\n      <td>Riverside International Raceway</td>\n      <td>California</td>\n      <td>USA</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>62</th>\n      <td>63</td>\n      <td>Sebring International Raceway</td>\n      <td>Florida</td>\n      <td>USA</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>68</th>\n      <td>69</td>\n      <td>Circuit of the Americas</td>\n      <td>Austin</td>\n      <td>USA</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>76</th>\n      <td>79</td>\n      <td>Miami International Autodrome</td>\n      <td>Miami</td>\n      <td>USA</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":4},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"The US has 12 circuits in the data. Eleven are labelled `USA`; only one, the Las Vegas Strip Street Circuit (circuitId 80), is labelled `United States`. The inconsistency therefore comes from a single circuit, and in cleaning (Part B) we relabel it as `USA`, the form used by all the other US circuits. Without this, Question 2 would treat races at this circuit as being in a different country from every other US race.\n\nThe `location` column is not consistent either: for some circuits it gives a city (Detroit, Austin, Miami), for others a whole state (California, Nevada, Florida). This does not affect our work. Question 1 identifies circuits by `circuitId` and Question 2 matches drivers to circuits by `country`, so `location` is not used anywhere and we leave it as it is.\n\nThe list also includes the Indianapolis Motor Speedway (circuitId 19), home of the Indianapolis 500. According to the F1 introduction, this American race counted in the F1 championship from 1950 to 1960 even though almost no regular F1 drivers took part, which would distort Question 2 on home races, so excluding it is a defensible choice. The races themselves are listed in the `races` table, so we come back to this there.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**constructors**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"df = raw[\"constructors\"]\ndisplay(df.head())\ndf.info()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.280246Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.280814Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.302802Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.280786Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.301942Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"   constructorId constructorRef        name nationality  \\\n0              1        mclaren     McLaren     British   \n1              2     bmw_sauber  BMW Sauber      German   \n2              3       w