umns:** all ten practice, qualifying and sprint date/time columns are `\\N` for these 2009 races. Our guess is that they were only recorded for recent seasons, which the audit will measure. They only describe the weekend's schedule, so we do not need them.\n\n4) **This table gives every race its time and place:** `year` and `date` place each race in history, which we need for the era comparisons in Questions 1 and 3 and for splitting the data by season; `circuitId` gives its location, which Questions 1 and 2 need. The brief notes that these questions need multi-hop joins rather than `results` alone, and `races` is where this information is stored; how the other tables reach it is checked in 1.2.\n\n5) **Available before the race?** Yes. The date, circuit and round of a race are fixed long in advance.\n\n**Do `races` and `seasons` cover the same years?** In 1.0 we saw that races run from 1950 to 2024 and that `seasons` has 75 rows, but the first and last year alone do not prove that every season in between has races. We compare the two sets of years.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"race_years = set(df[\"year\"])\nseason_years = set(raw[\"seasons\"][\"year\"])\n\nprint(\"Distinct years in races:\", len(race_years))\nprint(\"Same years in both tables:\", race_years == season_years)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.480105Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.480463Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.49796Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.48043Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-14T10:35:52.496954Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Distinct years in races: 75\nSame years in both tables: True\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":13},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"Every one of the 75 seasons from 1950 to 2024 has races, and `races` and `seasons` contain exactly the same years, so the two tables agree.\n\n**Which races were held at Indianapolis?** In `circuits` 