und the result of the same driver in the same race, so the two tables can always be combined through `raceId` and `driverId`.\n\nThe two tables disagree on the team in only 10 of these pairs, and all 10 follow the same pattern: the team is recorded as constructor 206 in `qualifying` and 209 in `results`, for the same three drivers in the same 5 races. So one team was given two different IDs in those races. This has two consequences for later steps: we combine `qualifying` and `results` on `raceId` and `driverId` only, never on `constructorId` as well, so these rows are not lost; and whenever we need a driver's team, we take it from `results`, so each driver has one team per race.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**constructor_results**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"df = raw[\"constructor_results\"]\ndf.info()\ndisplay(df.head())","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-14T12:33:09.01535Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-14T12:33:09.01628Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-14T12:33:09.033298Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-14T12:33:09.016247Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-14T12:33:09.032439Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"<class 'pandas.core.frame.DataFrame'>\nRangeIndex: 12625 entries, 0 to 12624\nData columns (total 5 columns):\n #   Column                Non-Null Count  Dtype  \n---  ------                --------------  -----  \n 0   constructorResultsId  12625 non-null  int64  \n 1   raceId                12625 non-null  int64  \n 2   constructorId         12625 non-null  int64  \n 3   points                12625 non-null  float64\n 4   status                12625 non-null  object \ndtypes: float64(1), int64(3), object(1)\nmemory usage: 493.3+ KB\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"   constructorResultsId  raceId  constructorId  points status\n0                     1      18              1    14.0     \\N\n1                     2      18        